      "worked": "Since $P(a,b)$ lies on $y=f(x)$, $f(a)=b$. Set $2-x=a$ to find the new horizontal coordinate.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=2-a\\\\y&=\\frac{3-2f(a)}{4}\\\\y&=\\frac{3-2b}{4}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe new coordinates are $\\left(2-a,\\frac{3-2b}{4}\\right)$.",
